# Copy to `.dev.vars` for local dev, or `.env.production` for one-time remote upload.
# Do not commit files that contain real values.
#
# Generate auth secret:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# OAuth apps:
#   GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → OAuth Apps
#     Authorization callback URL: https://ethanchang.io/api/auth/callback/github
#   Google → Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials
#     Authorized redirect URI: https://ethanchang.io/api/auth/callback/google
#
# Upload to Cloudflare Pages (production):
#   cp .dev.vars.example .env.production   # fill in real values
#   npm run setup:cloudflare

BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# Optional; defaults to request origin / https://ethanchang.io
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://ethanchang.io

GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Local dashboard (`npm run dev` → http://localhost:4321/dashboard).
# Production keeps these on Cloudflare Pages, not in this file.
# GITHUB_TOKEN_BLOG: fine-grained PAT for ethanchangit/ethanblog only
#   (Contents and Pull requests: read/write, Actions: read).
#   Same name as the Cursor Runtime Secret. GITHUB_TOKEN is also accepted.
#   Do not reuse the `gh` login token.
# STUDIO_SECRET: 32-byte key, base64. Same value as GitHub Actions.
# STUDIO_PASSWORD_HASH: from `npm run dashboard:password`. Localhost skips the password.
GITHUB_TOKEN_BLOG=
GITHUB_TOKEN=
STUDIO_SECRET=
STUDIO_PASSWORD_HASH=

# Guestbook mail does not use an API key. Pages binds GUESTBOOK to
# workers/guestbook (service binding). That Worker sends via Email Routing
# (EmailMessage) to hey@ethanchang.io. Local `astro dev` has no Worker —
# POST /api/comments returns 503. Enable Email Routing and verify
# hey@ethanchang.io as a destination before production deploy.
